  geometry: l1d_sets=128, l1d_ways=8, l2_sets=1024, l2_ways=4, llc_sets=1024, llc_ways=8
    because: Shrinking the L2 cache by halving its ways reduces its capacity and lowers its hit latency from 9 to 7 cycles, testing if the latency savings outweigh any increase in L2 misses.
  replacement: l2_replacement=lru, llc_replacement=srrip
    because: Since the LLC has a near-zero hit rate and acts as a latency bump, testing SRRIP at the LLC may better resist the scans causing thrashing than SHiP does.
  concurrency: l2_mshr=16, llc_mshr=32
    because: Reducing L2 MSHRs to 16 tests if aggressively limiting miss concurrency at the L2 can improve performance by throttling traffic to the highly congested and ineffective LLC.

